id: pm-x705zo
title: "As an MCP host or coding agent, I can discover pm capabilities and complete long-running context workflows through one current stateless protocol"
description: "An MCP consumer can discover versions and capabilities, invoke pm tools and resources, satisfy requested input, follow progress or task state, and resume at application-level handles without hidden connection state."
type: Story
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: agent-story,"area:mcp",discoverability,host-story,long-running,stateless
created_at: "2026-08-25T05:07:45.082Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-25T05:07:45.082Z"
deadline: "2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "The journey is executable over real stdio and Streamable HTTP transports; No successful operation depends on initialize state, an MCP session header, SSE redelivery, or undocumented server memory; Every response is token-bounded, deterministic where required, and exposes recovery when information is omitted; Input requests, task updates, progress, subscriptions, cancellation, and ordinary completion preserve one consistent state model; The packed and published agent transcript passes for npm, npx, bunx, and MCP consumers"
goal: One predictable current MCP experience for agents and hosts
objective: "Specify the end-to-end user outcome that all protocol, transport, task, resource, and conformance children jointly deliver"
value: Integrators need fewer bespoke pm adapters and agents receive compact explainable context through standard MCP flows
why_now: "The existing MCP experience depends on an obsolete handshake and does not expose the latest discovery, MRTR, subscription, cache, or task contracts"
parent: pm-rs9vry
risk: high
confidence: high
